   "confidence": "low",
   "notes": "Joshua Taylor Building, Market Passage side (faces NNW onto Market Passage; the walls.json 'Sidney Street' label is the address). Corner unit is David Clulow Opticians: a long dark-teal glazed shopfront with slim cast-iron colonnettes running ~13 m along the lane, then two small dark-blue units. Above: a white-rendered Georgian corner block (two sash bays, two upper floors) at the Sidney St end, then a taller buff-brick Victorian range with plain sashes in five columns over three floors. Upper-floor column positions estimated from raking views (703649 from 2008, 7393572 from 2023, both looking west from Sidney St)."
  },
